      "finding_id": "plain:authz:2",
      "cwe_id": "CWE-639",
      "explanation": "SearchResultSerializer.to_representation fetches a Document by id from instance['id'] without verifying the user has permission to view that specific document. The instance dict comes from search results which may not enforce ownership/permission checks. If the caller passes a malicious instance with an id the user shouldn't access, the document would be fetched and serialized.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "file": "src/documents/serialisers.py",
          "lines": [
            806,
            818
          ],
          "source": null,
          "content": "        doc = (\n            Document.objects.select_related(\n                \"correspondent\",\n                \"storage_path\",\n                \"document_type\",\n                \"owner\",\n            )\n            .prefetch_related(\"tags\", \"custom_fields\", \"notes\")\n            .get(id=instance[\"id\"])\n        )",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Add permission check before fetching the document: verify that request.user has view_document permission for the document with this id, potentially using get_objects_for_user_owner_aware or checking ownership.",
